<section class="section legal"><div class="wrap narrow"><div class="card"><h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
<p class="fine">Starting template — please have it reviewed by your legal adviser before launch. Last updated <?= e(fmt_dt(now(), 'd F Y')) ?>.</p>
<h2>What we collect</h2><p>When you register: full name, email address, phone number, age group, and optionally your state of residence, gender and a profile picture. When you take a quiz: your answers, scores, completion time, and browser events such as leaving the quiz page (shown to you before you start). We do not use your camera or microphone and we do not collect unrelated browsing information.</p>
<h2>How we use it</h2><p>To run quizzes and competitions fairly, calculate and publish results, contact you about programs you joined, and prepare anonymous or aggregated reports for partners and funders.</p>
<h2>Who can see it</h2><p>Authorised administrators can see participant records according to their role. Public results show only the identity format chosen by the organisation (for example first name and last initial, a participant ID, or an anonymous code). Email addresses and phone numbers are never shown publicly.</p>
<h2>Security and retention</h2><p>Passwords are stored as one-way hashes. Data is kept in a protected database with regular backups for as long as needed to run the program and meet reporting duties.</p>
<h2>Your choices</h2><p>You can edit your profile at any time and ask for correction or deletion of your personal data from your profile page. When personal data is deleted, quiz records may be kept without your identity.</p>
<h2>Contact</h2><p><?php $c = org_contact(); echo $c['email'] ? 'Email <a href="mailto:' . e($c['email']) . '">' . e($c['email']) . '</a>.' : 'Contact details are provided by the organisation.'; ?></p></div></div></section>
